# ShellCheck, which the step Shell scripts of scripts/check.sh runs and the images of
# the dev containers lack. .devcontainer/setup.sh installs it from the hash-pinned
# requirements.txt, which every repository gets as
# .devcontainer/shellcheck-requirements.txt. shellcheck-py has no dependencies and
# holds the binary in a wheel for Linux on x86-64; on Arm, as in Docker on a Mac with
# Apple silicon, pip builds it from its source, whose hash the lock file pins as well,
# and the build downloads the release of ShellCheck and checks its sha256. Renovate
# compiles it again with the command in the header of requirements.txt.
# https://github.com/Dennis-Otto/repo-blueprint
shellcheck-py
